# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Vue 3 + Vite project following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **File**: `package.json`
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package using npm with `--legacy-peer-deps` flag
- Note: Used `--legacy-peer-deps` to resolve peer dependency conflict with vue-router v5 (project uses v5.0.4, while @vercel/analytics expects v4)

### 2. Analytics Component Integration
- **File**: `src/App.vue`
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/vue'`
- Added `<Analytics />` component to the template
- Component is placed at the root level alongside `<RouterView />` to ensure analytics tracking across all routes

### 3. Lock File Updates
- **File**: `package-lock.json`
- Updated to include @vercel/analytics and its dependencies (256 packages added)

## Implementation Details

### Framework-Specific Approach
This is a **Vue 3 + Vite** project, so I followed the Vue-specific instructions from the official documentation:
- Imported Analytics component from `@vercel/analytics/vue`
- Added the component to the root App.vue file to enable tracking across the entire application

### Code Changes
The Analytics component was added to `App.vue` in a non-intrusive way:
- Preserved all existing imports and logic
- Maintained existing code structure and formatting
- The component requires no props or configuration for basic usage

## Verification

### Build Test
- Ran `npm run build` successfully
- Build completed in 1.26s with no errors
- All assets generated properly

## Next Steps

To complete the setup:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard (Analytics section)
3. Verify tracking is working by checking browser Network tab for `/_vercel/insights/*` requests

## Notes
- The @vercel/analytics package has a peer dependency on vue-router v4, but this project uses v5
- The installation required `--legacy-peer-deps` flag, which is acceptable as vue-router v5 maintains backward compatibility
- No breaking changes or warnings during build process
- Analytics will only start tracking once deployed to Vercel and enabled in the dashboard
